# Copy to .env (gitignored). Every variable says where its value comes from.
# `.worktreeinclude` copies .env into agent worktrees automatically.

# ─── runtime ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ENV=local

# Local Postgres and Redis come from `make up` (docker-compose.yml). On the
# host they listen on this checkout's DB_PORT / REDIS_PORT (`make env`), and
# the Makefile exports DATABASE_URL / REDIS_URL pointing at them, so leave
# these unset unless you are targeting a database that is not the local stack.
# Inside the containers the services are reached by name (see docker-compose.yml).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://bronze:bronze@localhost:5432/bronze
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ─── local stack (M0-03) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make up` derives a Compose project name and a host-port block from the
# checkout path (`make env`) so two worktrees can run stacks side by side.
# The Makefile reads your shell, never this file: `export DB_PORT=15432` (or
# `DB_PORT=15432 make up`) overrides a derived value, a line here does not,
# because `make up` exports its own values into Compose and a shell variable
# beats .env. Only a bare `docker compose up` reads these lines, and
# `.worktreeinclude` copies this file into every worktree, so a port fixed
# here would collide across checkouts. Leave them commented out.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=bronze-local
# DB_PORT=15432
# REDIS_PORT=16379
# API_PORT=18000
# Password of the local Postgres (user and database are both `bronze`),
# default `bronze` in the Makefile and in docker-compose.yml. Same rule:
# export it in your shell, not here, so the host-side DATABASE_URL (`make env`
# prints it masked) and the container agree. Set only here, `make up` ignores
# it while a bare `docker compose up` honours it, and the two stop agreeing.
# Local stack only; never a deployment secret.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Parallel SimC compile jobs for the worker image (~1.5 GB RAM each); 1 on a
# small VM. It is a build ARG, so changing it rebuilds the SimC layer. The one
# local-stack variable this file can carry for `make up`: the Makefile does
# not set it, so Compose falls through to this line.
# SIMC_BUILD_JOBS=2

# ─── Blizzard Battle.net API (M0-01, M0-05) ─────────────────────────────────
# Create a client at https://develop.battle.net/access/clients (any Battle.net
# account). Client-credentials only; no per-user OAuth needed for M0–M3.
BNET_CLIENT_ID=
BNET_CLIENT_SECRET=
BNET_REGION=us

# ─── Warcraft Logs API v2 (M5) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://www.warcraftlogs.com/api/clients — points budget is per client and
# shared with production; never used from tests or CI (ADR-0012).
WCL_CLIENT_ID=
WCL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Raider.IO (optional, M1+) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public endpoints need no key; a key raises the rate limit. https://raider.io/api
RAIDERIO_API_KEY=
